# Frontend build-time configuration. Copy to `.env`.
#
# These are INLINED INTO THE BUNDLE at build time, so they ship inside the APK.
# Addresses and flags only — never an API key. Secrets stay on the backend.
#
# Restart Metro with `--reset-cache` after changing this file: the values are
# baked in by Babel, so a warm cache keeps serving the old ones.

# Where the app should reach the backend.
#
# The Android emulator maps the host machine to 10.0.2.2, which is the default.
# A REAL DEVICE cannot resolve that or "localhost" — set API_HOST to your
# machine's LAN address, e.g. 192.168.1.20, with the phone on the same Wi-Fi.
# API_HOST=192.168.1.20
# API_PORT=8000

# Or override the whole URL, e.g. for a staging deployment.
# API_BASE_URL=https://staging.example.com/v1

# Serve local fixtures instead of the backend. Development builds only:
# release builds ignore this, so mock data can never reach a real user.
# USE_MOCK=false

# Self-hosted LiveKit, if you are running it. Same LAN-address caveat.
# LIVEKIT_URL=ws://192.168.1.20:7880
